Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the Solr slave performing a full replication of the entire index after the master node was restarted, even when the index had not changed. This behavior was likely due to the replication logic not properly checking the state of the index or the conditions under which replication should occur, particularly in a SolrCloud environment where ZooKeeper is used for coordination.

